            <ArticleTitle>Commissural myelotomy for intractable cancer pain: report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>151-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We describe two patients with cancer-related low back and bilateral lower extremity pain that failed pharmacologic treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">In both cases, commissural myelotomy provided significant pain relief. The role of myelotomy in the management of cancer pain is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
